// FROZEN FIXTURE: the "before" shape of the stalker. Do not edit, do not fix, do not use in a level or host.
//
// This is the stalker domain as it was before the restructure of 2026-10-18: ported one-to-one from an earlier
// prototype, then grown branch by branch. It is kept as the known bad shape, next to the live
// src/examples/stalker/stalker.domain (the "after"). What is wrong with it: docs/htn-guidance.md, Domain design
// ("Our domains against this"); the experiment and its numbers: the Domain variants section of docs/htn-level-metrics.md. In short:
//   - a 21-branch root with almost no hierarchy (18 of 21 branches primitive-only), 2 method levels in all;
//   - five top-level branches that only do memory bookkeeping (forget_unnoticed, forget_stale_noise,
//     forget_noise_before_sighting, ignore_player_noise_on_route, drop_focus), plus the !forget_noise that opens
//     chase_ignoring_noise: each costs a plan and a tick, and a held noise makes the chase cut and restart itself;
//   - four copied multi-step tails (the longest 6 steps) instead of compound tasks with parameters;
//   - branches correct only because filters sit above them (14 specific-first pairs).
//
// Kept for:
//   (a) the decision-equivalence test, test/npc/tiered-equivalence.test.ts: the live domain against this one,
//       decision by decision (and the random-visitor diff, node scripts/htn-variant-diff.mjs, variant 'flat');
//   (b) the lint known-bad fixture: test/tools/htn-lint.test.ts ("the known bad examples") and the lint baseline
//       (test/tools/htn-lint.baseline.json) expect the structure warnings to fire here; htn-lint.json keeps its host
//       lists and relaxes no rule on it (docs/htn-lint.md, "The scene's htn-lint.json, and why");
//   (c) the before / after teaching pair (docs/htn-guidance.md, Domain design).
// Its generated module (stalker_flat.htn.ts) exists for those tests and tools only; nothing under src/ imports it.
//
// ---- the original header ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Stalker: walk a short route or stand; once watching, a target in sight is noticed: a beat, the head
// turns, the body follows, then it runs at the target. A target that comes close is noticed even before
// it watches. Caught: stand over it. Lost: go to where it was last seen (stand longer at a shelter door),
// look around, give up and walk away, then despawn. A route walked to its end despawns too.
// Hearing: an impact heard while it is not hunting a target it sees makes it start, turn toward the
// sound, listen, then walk there and look around; then it resumes what it did (route, search, standing).
// While investigating it is focused: its sight narrows to a cone ahead (host), so a target behind it can
// slip past and one in front of it is noticed. Seen while it hunts it, a noise is dropped: the chase goes
// on. A noise heard before it last saw its target is stale news and dropped too.
// It also hears the player (steps, running, landings, voice; the host scales how far): the same
// investigation turns it toward whoever made the noise, so sight takes over. A loud noise close by makes
// it spin round at once. Hunting someone it lost, their footsteps make it hurry after them without the
// start. While it investigates, a newer footstep re-targets it without another start. On a scripted route
// before it watches (a reveal), the player's own noises are ignored.
//
// Facts, synced by the host every tick (htn-planner/npc/blackboard.ts, stalker-actions.ts):
//   (now ?time)                          agent clock, float seconds
//   (self_position ?position)            (x y z) floats, feet
//   (target_visible ?target ?position)   one row per detected target
//   (last_seen ?target ?position ?time)  memory of a lost target until forgotten
//   (waypoint ?index ?position)          route, int index; may be empty (standing)
//   (waypoint_count ?count)
//   (current_waypoint ?index)            next waypoint; == count once the route is walked
//   (watch_point ?index)                 waypoint after which it starts watching (on the path)
//   (route_loop yes)                     static: the route is a patrol loop (never walked off)
//   (waypoint_look ?index ?seconds)      static: on a patrol, stop and look around at this waypoint
//   (waypoint_face ?index ?position)     static: on a patrol, peer toward this point there with the head, the
//                                        body staying (the lane: where the player comes from)
//   (watching yes)                       a visible target can be noticed (set by !watch or at spawn)
//   (noticed ?target)                    it has noticed it (set by !notice)
//   (target_close ?target)               visible and close: noticed even when not watching
//   (target_in_front ?target)            visible and roughly ahead: no head / body turn needed
//   (target_sheltered ?target)           the target hides in a shelter (host shelter check)
//   (caught ?target)                     set by !catch
//   (gave_up ?target)                    set by !give_up, with (exit_point ?position)
//   (heard_noise ?kind ?position ?time ?loudness)  the latest heard noise; ?loudness = perceived 0..1
//   (player_noise ?kind)                 static, set at spawn: kinds the player makes (steps, run, land, voice)
//   (focus ?time)                        investigating the noise heard at ?time (set by !hear / !refocus)
//
// Primitives, executed by the host (htn-planner/npc/actions.ts, stalker-actions.ts):
//   (!move_to ?position ?gait)     gait: walk | hurry | run
//   (!chase ?target)               run at the live target until within catch radius
//   (!catch ?target)               catch: the host fails the player
//   (!look_around ?seconds)
//   (!peer ?position ?seconds)     the body stays, the head (and its sight) turns toward the point and peers there
//   (!forget ?target)
//   (!set_waypoint ?index)
//   (!watch)                       start watching
//   (!notice ?target)              noticed (host cue)
//   (!stand ?seconds)              stand still (idle clip)
//   (!head_turn ?target)           HeadTurnLeft, body still
//   (!body_turn ?target)           BodyTurnLeft, the body yaw follows the clip (or a quick turn)
//   (!give_up ?target ?position)   stop hunting; pick an exit away from the target
//   (!despawn)
//   (!hear ?position ?time)        heard a noise: start (host cue), focus on it (sets focus)
//   (!refocus ?time)               focus on a newer noise without the start (no cue)
//   (!face ?position)              turn in place toward a point (PatrolTurn, slower than a chase turn)
//   (!face ?position quick)        the same at the chase turn rate (startled)
//   (!forget_noise ?time)          drop the heard noise if it is still the one heard at ?time
//   (!unfocus)                     investigation over: all-around sight again (clears focus)

(:domain StalkerFlat top_level_domain

    (:constants StalkerSettings
        (catch_pause 2.0)
        (look_around_time 3.0)
        (door_wait 4.0)
        (notice_pause 0.4)
        (glare_time 1.0)
        (idle_wait 1.0)
        (startle_time 0.5)
        (noise_listen_time 1.2)
        (noise_look_time 4.0)
        (noise_memory_span 30.0)
        (loud_noise 0.6)
    )

    (:method (behave) top_level_method

        (stand_over_caught
            (and
                (caught ?any_target)
            )
            (
                (!stand @idle_wait)
            )
        )

        // Giving up is final: it walks off even if the target shows up again.
        (leave
            (and
                (gave_up ?any_target)
                (exit_point ?position)
            )
            (
                (!move_to ?position walk)
                (!despawn)
            )
        )

        // It sees the one it hunts: a noise now does not distract it.
        (chase_ignoring_noise
            (and
                (noticed ?target)
                (target_visible ?target ?any_position)
                (heard_noise ?any_kind ?any_noise_position ?heard_at ?any_loudness)
            )
            (
                (!forget_noise ?heard_at)
                (!chase ?target)
                (!catch ?target)
                (!stand @catch_pause)
            )
        )

        (chase_noticed_target
            (and
                (noticed ?target)
                (target_visible ?target ?any_position)
            )
            (
                (!chase ?target)
                (!catch ?target)
                (!stand @catch_pause)
            )
        )

        (notice_seen_target
            (and
                (watching ?any_flag)
                (target_visible ?target ?any_position)
                (not (noticed ?target))
            )
            (
                (notice_target ?target)
            )
        )

        (notice_close_target
            (and
                (target_close ?target)
                (not (noticed ?target))
            )
            (
                (notice_target ?target)
            )
        )

        // Seen in passing before it watched: not its business yet.
        (forget_unnoticed
            (and
                (last_seen ?target ?any_position ?any_seen_at)
                (not (noticed ?target))
            )
            (
                (!forget ?target)
            )
        )

        (forget_stale_noise
            (and
                (now ?time)
                (heard_noise ?any_kind ?any_position ?heard_at ?any_loudness)
                (> (- ?time ?heard_at) @noise_memory_span)
            )
            (
                (!forget_noise ?heard_at)
            )
        )

        // Heard while it still saw the one it hunts (e.g. thrown during the chase): stale news.
        (forget_noise_before_sighting
            (and
                (noticed ?target)
                (last_seen ?target ?any_position ?seen_at)
                (heard_noise ?any_kind ?any_noise_position ?heard_at ?any_loudness)
                (< ?heard_at ?seen_at)
            )
            (
                (!forget_noise ?heard_at)
            )
        )

        (drop_focus
            (and
                (focus ?any_time)
                (not (heard_noise ?any_kind ?any_position ?any_heard_at ?any_loudness))
            )
            (
                (!unfocus)
            )
        )

        // On a scripted route before it watches (a reveal): the reveal is not cut short by the player's own
        // noise; any other noise still draws it off.
        (ignore_player_noise_on_route
            (and
                (watch_point ?any_index)
                (not (watching ?any_flag))
                (heard_noise ?kind ?any_position ?heard_at ?any_loudness)
                (player_noise ?kind)
            )
            (
                (!forget_noise ?heard_at)
            )
        )

        // Hunting the one it lost and hearing them: no start, a quick turn, hurry to the sound. Facing
        // it, its sight takes over (the chase branches above).
        (track_heard_target
            (and
                (noticed ?any_target)
                (heard_noise ?kind ?position ?heard_at ?any_loudness)
                (player_noise ?kind)
            )
            (
                (!refocus ?heard_at)
                (!face ?position quick)
                (!move_to ?position hurry)
                (!look_around @noise_look_time)
                (!forget_noise ?heard_at)
                (!unfocus)
            )
        )

        // Already turned toward this noise (a replan mid-investigation): go on without the start again.
        (continue_investigation
            (and
                (heard_noise ?any_kind ?position ?heard_at ?any_loudness)
                (focus ?heard_at)
            )
            (
                (!watch)
                (!face ?position)
                (!move_to ?position walk)
                (!look_around @noise_look_time)
                (!forget_noise ?heard_at)
                (!unfocus)
            )
        )

        // Investigating, and the player makes another noise (the next footstep): re-target it without
        // another start; it turns to it and watches, so the one who made it ends up in its sight.
        (retarget_investigation
            (and
                (focus ?any_focus)
                (heard_noise ?kind ?position ?heard_at ?any_loudness)
                (player_noise ?kind)
            )
            (
                (!refocus ?heard_at)
                (!watch)
                (!face ?position)
                (!move_to ?position walk)
                (!look_around @noise_look_time)
                (!forget_noise ?heard_at)
                (!unfocus)
            )
        )

        // A loud noise close by (a landing behind it, an impact at its feet): it spins round at once and
        // watches; the next plan notices whoever is there.
        (startled_by_loud_noise
            (and
                (heard_noise ?any_kind ?position ?heard_at ?loudness)
                (>= ?loudness @loud_noise)
            )
            (
                (!hear ?position ?heard_at)
                (!face ?position quick)
                (!watch)
            )
        )

        // A new noise: start, a beat, turn to it, listen; then it watches. The plan ends there, so the
        // next plan notices a target now in its (narrowed) sight before it walks off to the sound.
        (investigate_noise
            (and
                (heard_noise ?any_kind ?position ?heard_at ?any_loudness)
            )
            (
                (!hear ?position ?heard_at)
                (!stand @startle_time)
                (!face ?position)
                (!stand @noise_listen_time)
                (!watch)
            )
        )

        (search_at_shelter
            (and
                (noticed ?target)
                (last_seen ?target ?position ?any_seen_at)
                (target_sheltered ?target)
            )
            (
                (!move_to ?position hurry)
                (!stand @door_wait)
                (!look_around @look_around_time)
                (!forget ?target)
                (!give_up ?target ?position)
            )
        )

        (search_last_seen
            (and
                (noticed ?target)
                (last_seen ?target ?position ?any_seen_at)
            )
            (
                (!move_to ?position hurry)
                (!look_around @look_around_time)
                (!forget ?target)
                (!give_up ?target ?position)
            )
        )

        (walked_off
            (and
                (waypoint_count ?count)
                (> ?count 0)
                (current_waypoint ?index)
                (>= ?index ?count)
            )
            (
                (!despawn)
            )
        )

        (walk_route
            (and
                (current_waypoint ?index)
                (waypoint ?index ?position)
            )
            (
                (!move_to ?position walk)
                (&after_waypoint ?index)
            )
        )

        (idle
            ()
            (
                (!stand @idle_wait)
            )
        )
    )

    // Deferred: on reaching a waypoint. At the watch point it starts watching; the plan then ends, so
    // the next plan already sees a target in sight and notices it right there on the path.
    (:method (after_waypoint ?inp_index)

        (at_watch_point
            (and
                (watch_point ?inp_index)
            )
            (
                (!set_waypoint (++ ?inp_index))
                (!watch)
            )
        )

        // A patrol: the route loops; at a waypoint with a look it stops and looks around (its sight a cone
        // there: the sweep is what can find the player). At a waypoint with a face point it peers the way the
        // player comes: only the head turns, the body stays in profile (no reason to turn before it noticed
        // anyone, but it peers).
        (face_and_look_on_patrol
            (and
                (route_loop ?any_flag)
                (waypoint_look ?inp_index ?seconds)
                (waypoint_face ?inp_index ?position)
                (waypoint_count ?count)
            )
            (
                (!peer ?position ?seconds)
                (!set_waypoint (% (++ ?inp_index) ?count))
            )
        )
        (look_on_patrol
            (and
                (route_loop ?any_flag)
                (waypoint_look ?inp_index ?seconds)
                (waypoint_count ?count)
            )
            (
                (!look_around ?seconds)
                (!set_waypoint (% (++ ?inp_index) ?count))
            )
        )
        (next_on_patrol
            (and
                (route_loop ?any_flag)
                (waypoint_count ?count)
            )
            (
                (!set_waypoint (% (++ ?inp_index) ?count))
            )
        )
        (next_waypoint
            ()
            (
                (!set_waypoint (++ ?inp_index))
            )
        )
    )

    (:method (notice_target ?inp_target)

        // Already facing it (e.g. standing in a doorway): a short glare, then the run.
        (already_facing
            (and
                (target_in_front ?inp_target)
            )
            (
                (!notice ?inp_target)
                (!stand @glare_time)
            )
        )

        (turn_to_target
            ()
            (
                (!notice ?inp_target)
                (!stand @notice_pause)
                (!head_turn ?inp_target)
                (!body_turn ?inp_target)
            )
        )
    )
)
